pkg:Evidence_v1_8_1 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.8.1 (PATCH release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "PATCH: user asked for an explicit fit-gap comparing the Epic against the Scope. Ran it bidirectionally rather than re-asserting existing links: Scope->Epic (built a table mapping every Deliverable to whichever Stories actually address it) and Epic->Scope (re-read every Story's wantsCapability/soThat against real Scope content, and checked all 3 Exclusions against every Story's text). Found one real, previously-undetected gap: Deliverable_DisclosedLimitsPreserved had zero Story-level coverage -- the disclosure obligation (Amplitude figures, GitLab COI note) was named extensively at Mission/Scope/Goal/Objective level throughout, but no Story anywhere planned how the 2 disclosures actually get carried into the new corpus-instantiated artifact, a genuine risk since that artifact is built from scratch. Fixed: widened STORY-1's scope (the natural home, since disclosures are CITATIONS-schema content, the field STORY-1 already targets) to explicitly require them as real corpus entries, and added pursuesObjective on ObjDisclosedLimitsVisible. satisfiesDeliverable correctly checked and found empty (0/3, honest since nothing is Done). One real editing error caught mid-fix (a str_replace initially dropped STORY-1's partOf link and mangled STORY-2's opening declaration) -- caught immediately by re-parsing before proceeding, not assumed to have worked. Re-verified: pipeline order unaffected (property edits, no new tracked-type subjects), full SHACL 0 violations."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "ff6171a8d14f114012b3b6c05284ab4da527dc5f932d28c9a9f640f55bc99cf2"^^xsd:string .
